  "worked_solution": "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0)^{2}}{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{4} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ \\pm \\frac{x-1}{2} & =z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $xz$-plane with equations $z=\\frac{x-1}{2}$ and $z=\\frac{1-x}{2}.$ \n\nTo find the point of intersection of both lines, we equate the right-hand sides. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-1}{2} & =\\frac{1-x}{2} \\\\ x-1 & =1-x \\\\ 2x & =2 \\\\ x & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1$ in the equation of the first line and solving for $z,$ we obtain $z=\\frac{1-1}{2}=0.$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(1,0,0).$",
